An unstubbed macro is genuinely executed through the CLI's own subprocess boundary: the
config declares `echo 1` as the argv, and the only way the key can read `1` is that the
command ran and its stdout was captured.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    probe: ["echo", "1"]
-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md probe="{{ macro('core.macros.probe') }}"
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ---
 title: Foo
+probe: 1
 ---
 # Body
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: probe=1
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
probe: 1
---
# Body
